---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About · Lecheeel" description="Lecheeel's interests in embedded systems, FPGA control, PCB design, and Android internals.">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">about</h1>
  <div class="prose prose-slate mt-8 max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
    <p>
      I'm Lecheeel. I work on embedded systems and software, with an interest
      in how computational models, control logic, and hardware fit together.
    </p>
    <p>
      My embedded work involves microcontroller firmware, digital interfaces,
      circuit design, and PCB layout. I'm interested in high-speed layout,
      differential pair routing, impedance control, and signal integrity,
      including how clock distribution and return paths affect a design.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm particularly interested in FPGA-based control for ultrasonic phased
      arrays, including multichannel phase synthesis, synchronized waveform
      generation, and coordinated parameter updates across an array.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm also exploring the acoustic side: wave superposition, phase
      compensation, acoustic radiation forces, and the relationship between a
      calculated field and a stable trapping position. Three-dimensional
      particle manipulation brings these topics together with trajectory
      generation, array calibration, and experimental measurement.
    </p>
    <p>
      On the software side, I've been studying Android platform internals
      through AOSP, framework services, Binder IPC, and HAL interfaces. I'm
      interested in how service lifecycles, process boundaries, and hardware
      interfaces shape system behavior. Related areas include GNSS data
      processing, NMEA parsing, and the GKI architecture, including the Kernel
      Module Interface (KMI) and vendor modules.
    </p>
    <p>
      Across these areas, I like tracing the details that affect a system's
      behavior, whether that's timing between output channels, calibration
      errors in an array, or a request moving through Android's framework
      and kernel interfaces.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is where I document selected work and explain the technical
      details behind it. You can find my public repositories on
      <a href="https://github.com/Lecheeel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      or contact me by <a href="mailto:ryancuee@gmail.com">email</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
